From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 21:16:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8998-google-wahoo: mark ramoops region
 no-map

CONFIG_PSTORE_RAM has been enabled and this board already carries a
ramoops node at the vendor's proven region (0xb0000000, 2 MB), but the
node is missing the no-map property that every other in-tree ramoops
node sets. Without it the region stays part of the kernel's normal
linear map instead of being excluded from it, which is the wrong
model for memory meant to survive a warm reset untouched.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-wahoo.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-wahoo.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-wahoo.dtsi
index 80094685362c..388781562490 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-wahoo.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-wahoo.dtsi
@@ -86,6 +86,7 @@ ramoops: ramoops@b0000000 {
 			record-size = <0x20000>;
 			console-size = <0x100000>;
 			pmsg-size = <0x80000>;
+			no-map;
 		};
 
 		zap_shader_region: memory@f6900000 {
